  "body": "## Behavior changes\r\n- PandaScript: `page.evaluate()` now returns a promise, like `page.goto()`. Saved scripts need `await` in front of every `page.evaluate(...)`. Several evaluates can now run at once with `Promise.all`.\r\n- `--v8-gc-hint-floor-mb` is renamed `--v8-gc-request-min-mb`. The old name still works but is deprecated.\r\n- New `--v8-gc-auto-min-mb`, default 32: V8 doesn't start a full GC on its own below this heap size. `0` keeps V8's default.\r\n- `classify`, `acceptCookies` and `login` can use Gemini, but only with `LIGHTPANDA_DECISION_PROVIDER=gemini`. TypeSafe stays the default.\r\n- `agent --save` replays a read-only script once before writing it. If the replay fails or returns nothing, the model gets one turn to fix the script, and the first script is kept, with a warning, when the fix doesn't replay. Scripts that act on a page are written unchecked.\r\n- A fetch or XHR whose connection drops before the end of a `Content-Length` or chunked body now fails, instead of resolving as a complete 200.\r\n- `history.pushState`/`replaceState` to a URL of another origin throws a `SecurityError`.\r\n- Responses served from the HTTP cache now go through CORS checks.\r\n- `document.currentScript` is `null` while a module runs.\r\n- The `goto` timeout (script API and MCP tool) now bounds the navigation wait, even while a parser-blocking script is loading.\r\n- Mouse hit testing skips `inert` subtrees.\r\n\r\n## Layout\r\n- More realistic `top` and `height`, with awareness of positioned boxes, tables and text\r\n- `display: grid` support\r\n- `em`, `rem` and basic `calc()` lengths; `min-height` and `max-height`\r\n- Text wrapping uses the computed width\r\n- Hit testing: positioned boxes are above the normal flow, negative `z-index` below it\r\n- Layout, hit testing and bounding rects are much faster (style caches are cleared only where a change can reach)\r\n\r\n## New Web APIs\r\n- `NavigateEvent.intercept()`\r\n- `ReadableStream.tee()` and `values()`\r\n- `XMLHttpRequest.upload` progress events\r\n- `Attr.specified`\r\n\r\n## Web API behavior / fixes\r\n- XHR: re-opening a request in flight doesn't fire `abort`/`loadend`; `responseType = 'document'` is ignored in a worker\r\n- WebSocket `close()` while connecting moves to `CLOSING` and queues a `close` event\r\n- `Request` keeps the case of methods other than the six standard ones\r\n- `fetch` with `redirect: 'manual'` keeps the URL\r\n- The `formdata` event gets its own copy of the `FormData`\r\n- `ResizeObserver` starts from a size of -1×-1\r\n- IndexedDB: a pending request keeps its JS object until its event fires (fixes Zone.js apps)\r\n\r\n## CDP\r\n- Playwright can use the default context before any page: `context.addCookies()` works, and `page.close()` on the startup page no longer hangs\r\n- `DOM.getBoxModel` returns Chrome's error for an element under `display: none`\r\n- `Accessibility.getFullAXTree` reports the selected option's label as a combobox value\r\n- `LP.dump` `withFrames` option: include iframe content in the HTML dump\r\n- Crash fix in request interception on an aborted transfer\r\n\r\n## WebDriver\r\n- `/alert` commands answer `no such alert`\r\n- Element `/displayed`, `/computedrole` and `/computedlabel`\r\n- Shadow root endpoints: `/element/{id}/shadow`, `/shadow/{id}/element`, `/shadow/{id}/elements`\r\n- Sessions accept `acceptInsecureCerts`\r\n\r\n## BiDi\r\n- `script.addPreloadScript` and `script.removePreloadScript` (no `arguments` yet)\r\n\r\n## Tools / MCP / Agent\r\n- `lightpanda mcp --tools goto,tree,...` exposes only the named tools; `--list-tools` prints every name\r\n- MCP over HTTP: memory is returned to the OS when a session ends, and the idle default session closes its pages after `--http-session-timeout`\r\n- PandaScript `page.getCookies()`\r\n- `lightpanda run` and `agent` now apply `--cookie` and `--cookie-jar`\r\n- Markdown: definition list terms and details go on their own lines\r\n\r\n## Performance / memory\r\n- Stylesheets with `--load-resources stylesheet` are preloaded in parallel\r\n- Smaller CSS DOM: rules are created only when JS reads them, `@media`/`@layer`/`@supports` parsed once\r\n- Smaller nodes and elements (a `div` goes from 80 to 64 bytes)\r\n- The page HTML is held once instead of three times (CNN peak memory 65 MB → 54 MB)\r\n- `fetch()` takes the response body instead of copying it\r\n- Semantic tree uses less memory (HTML spec: 249 MB → 154 MB)\r\n- Faster `getComputedStyle`, `nodeList[i]` and object wrapping",
